{"run_id":"live-brownfield-2","seq":7,"ts":"2026-11-02T17:12:58.964+00:00","type":"DECISION_RECORDED","stage":"requirements","payload":{"artifact":{"name":"requirements","version":1,"sha":"d55ce9d63e3fec0ddf6e073db476ba8ed9a8102fe0421e4f8cb7b40f420cc56a"},"topic":"How should the test establish that the second operation is waiting specifically on the target row lock?","choice":"Use existing database-native lock-wait visibility where available, or equivalent test-only instrumentation that can identify the second operation as blocked on the target link row. Do not treat a start signal or lack of completion alone as proof.","rationale":"Directly observing the database wait is the least invasive conventional way to prove the claimed lock interleaving, and it avoids production-code changes.","source":"assumption"},"prev_hash":"d2be29f069a3a76cea8d0292834acbf5bc53841b57077062dec8fb280cc6a731","hash":"0fdd9cab017542a30e8a0bf9967c463f7625f10efd55a8ead2c18fe96ca28fd1"}
